A table and one of its columns renamed at once: the new table is made from
the old one's rows, its new column filled from the old one's column.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, served TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch', 'noon');

== after
-- @drop table menu
-- @from table meal = menu
-- @from column meal name = title
CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, served TEXT) STRICT;

== query
SELECT id, name, served FROM meal

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `meal`: `menu` aside, to make it from
    ALTER TABLE "menu" RENAME TO "roux_old_menu"
  table `meal`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE meal (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, served TEXT) STRICT
  table `meal`: its rows, by id, name = title, served
    INSERT INTO "meal" ("id", "name", "served") SELECT "id", (
    title
    ), "served" FROM "roux_old_menu"
  table `meal`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_menu"

== rows
1 | lunch | noon
